{"run_id": "20260815T104348-hepkg-48526", "qid": "gen-concept-0e21c7a8", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "76ac05498582", "git_sha": "b6ce7b2-dirty", "question": "Count the analyses that estimate the background Diboson ($WW$, $WZ$, $ZZ$) background.", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 28 distinct analyses that estimate the Diboson ($WW$, $WZ$, $ZZ$) background. \n\nThis includes 36 distinct facts and 38 assertions across these analyses. \n\nTo provide more context, the 28 analyses cover a range of specific Diboson backgrounds, including:\n- Non-resonant WW diboson background\n- ZZ and WZ diboson background (multilepton)\n- Non-WW diboson background (WZ/gamma*, ZZ/gamma*, Wgamma, Zgamma)\n- SM diboson background in RJR selection\n- Diboson background (2$\\ell$OS channel, combined)\n- Other subdominant SM backgrounds (e.g., tZ, tWZ, ttW, tth, ttWW, tttt, ttt, Wh, Zh, single top, diboson in 1l)\n- Background from jets misidentified as tau_h candidates (QCD multijet, W+jets, ttbar, diboson)\n- Rare irreducible SM backgrounds (triboson, Higgs, other rare processes)\n\nEach of these analyses provides specific insights into the Diboson background, contributing to the overall understanding of the background in high-energy physics experiments.\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2012.03799", "2102.01444", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2109.13808", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Diboson", "kind": "background"}, "rows": 21, "error": null, "seconds": 36.508}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count"